WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.600
Saved a hundred great articles,
but go blank when a real problem hits?

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.360
Your collection keeps growing.
How can your understanding grow with it?

3
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.380
Incremind, a personal memory assistant.

4
00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:15.460
Let's use two learning texts
to go from reading to practical use.

5
00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:20.160
Industry research, project ideas,
podcast notes, or a new learning method:

6
00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.320
build up each topic's knowledge separately.

7
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:27.300
Choose the learning project.
Add the first text and click Send.

8
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:30.400
After processing, open the insight
on a fixed review schedule.

9
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.340
Check its content, then click Confirm.

10
00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:35.420
It becomes our baseline
for comparing new information.

11
00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:38.880
Back in the Workbench,
add the second text to the input box.

12
00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:42.800
It covers active recall
and how to adjust review intervals.

13
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.160
Check the text, then click Send.

14
00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:48.420
The system processes this actual material.

15
00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:52.120
The original is kept; you can revisit
the organized note and summary.

16
00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:55.020
After processing, open the extracted insights.

17
00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:59.460
What does this add
to the method we've already saved?

18
00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:04.140
Open the insight on review intervals,
then the earlier insight it relates to.

19
00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:06.700
The earlier insight sets fixed review dates.

20
00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:10.000
The second text says
a fixed schedule is just a starting point.

21
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.880
Adjust it based on how well
you recall each time.

22
00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:17.320
Compare old and new on the same question,
and the change becomes clear:

23
00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:21.380
use your own recall performance
to decide when to review next.

24
00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:23.260
Now it's our turn to choose.

25
00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:25.360
We want a better review schedule.

26
00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:29.060
First, look for useful steps,
then check when they apply.

27
00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:32.260
If this adjustment is worth keeping,
click Confirm.

28
00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:37.120
The insight becomes active.
The earlier insight is still there to view.

29
00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:40.640
Open another method.
The text says: recall the answer yourself,

30
00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:44.220
then flip the card, check,
and record how well you recalled it.

31
00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:47.040
This insight explains what to do
during review.

32
00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:50.300
Check its content and conditions,
then confirm it separately.

33
00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:52.940
We decide what to keep each time.

34
00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:55.200
Both new insights are now confirmed.

35
00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:58.480
No need to add the two texts again.
Return to the Workbench.

36
00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:02.560
Ask a new question:
How should I adjust fixed review intervals?

37
00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:04.680
Check your question, then click Send.

38
00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:08.880
The new insight on adjusting for difficulty
is now in the answer's context.

39
00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:14.340
From the texts, the answer gives steps:
recall, check, record results, adjust intervals.

40
00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:17.000
What you read now feeds
into what you do next.

41
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:20.720
The answer includes citations.
Open a link to the original

42
00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:22.780
to return to its exact passage.

43
00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:26.740
Verify the advice's source
and whether it reflects the material accurately.

44
00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:31.440
The materials stay saved,
and new understanding grows little by little.

45
00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.720
Compare, choose, confirm,
and ask your next question.

46
00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:38.240
Connect what you've read
to the things you actually need to do.

47
00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:41.760
Incremind connects what you've read carefully

48
00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:44.200
to the next problem you need to solve.
